# Never let these into the Docker build context - a stray developer .env
# with real secrets getting COPY'd into an image layer is exactly the kind
# of leak that's easy to miss until it's in a public registry. Confirmed this
# was a real risk: Next's standalone build output copies any .env file it
# finds next to it (see docs/production-readiness-audit.md).
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

node_modules
.next
.tools
.git
.github

npm-debug.log*
*.log

test-results
playwright-report
coverage

.DS_Store
